# Trivy suppression list.
#
# Keep this file present (workflows pass `--ignorefile .trivyignore`); add new
# suppressions here with a dated `exp:` and a rationale. Each entry must be
# time-boxed so a suppression cannot silently outlive the condition it accepts.
# Fast Gate and the main/tag Security gate validate metadata and expiry.
# Required comment block immediately before each entry (no blank line):
# exception-owner: @responsible-owner
# exception-claim: false-positive|not-affected|protected-by-control|accepted-risk|under-investigation
# exception-scope: exact artifact/component/platform affected
# exception-evidence: docs/engineering/TECHNICAL-RISK-REGISTER.md#evidence-anchor
# The register records the claim, tests/CI, residual risk and approval; metadata
# alone is not evidence. Expiry is 00:00 UTC on the named date.
#
# Historical note: the former entries masked docker/docker SDK CVEs reachable
# only through the legacy culvert-updater sidecar module (RISK-ACC-1 / DEBT-008).
# That module was removed, so nothing imports docker/docker and those masks are
# gone.

# CVE-2026-14456 expired 2026-09-15; removed rather than renewed. Vendor
# advisory/package evidence and exact artifact limits are recorded in RISK-006.
